@* HelpPlanningPage: help topic "Planning reviews" at "/help/planning-reviews". Static text and screenshots. *@
@page "/help/planning-reviews"

<HelpTopicFrame Slug="planning-reviews">
    <section class="card">
        <p>If a repository of the project has a <code>.reviewmark.yaml</code> file that lists review-sets, you can create several
            reviews at once. On the project page choose <strong>Plan reviews from a repository</strong>, enter the
            head revision, choose what to compare with, and press <strong>Show plan</strong>. Tick the sets you want and
            create them. A set that was already filed at the same revisions is not offered twice.</p>
        <p>Under <strong>What to review</strong> the default is
            <strong>Changes since the last approved review of each set</strong>. A review counts as approved when every
            reviewer has signed it and no thread is open. A set that has no approved review yet is planned as a full
            review, and its note says so.</p>
        <figure class="help-figure">
            <img class="help-shot" src="/help/planning-reviews-1.png" loading="lazy"
                 alt="The Plan reviews page with the repository, head revision and what-to-review choices, and the Show plan button." />
            <figcaption>The Plan reviews page of a project.</figcaption>
        </figure>
    </section>
</HelpTopicFrame>
